---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Callout from '@components/Callout.astro';
import { CATEGORIES } from '@data/categories';
import { SITE } from '@data/site';
import { categoryUrl } from '@lib/url';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="What this site is, how it is organized, and how views are handled.">
  <article class="container page">
    <header class="head">
      <p class="label eyebrow">About this book</p>
      <h1>How Commonplace works</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="prose has-dropcap">
      <p>
        From the Renaissance on, serious readers kept a <em>commonplace book</em>: a bound volume
        where they copied passages worth remembering, sketched arguments, and drew the diagrams that
        helped them see a subject whole. It was not a diary and not a treatise. It was a working
        reference, organized under headings, meant to be opened again.
      </p>
      <p>
        This site is that book for theology. Charts, timelines, word studies, and notes are filed
        under a handful of shelves so that anything can be found again in a few seconds.
      </p>

      <h2>The shelves</h2>
      <dl class="shelves">
        {
          CATEGORIES.map((c) => (
            <div class={`shelf accent-${c.accent}`}>
              <dt>
                <span class="initial" aria-hidden="true">{c.initial}</span>
                <a href={categoryUrl(c.slug)}>{c.name}</a>
              </dt>
              <dd>{c.description}</dd>
            </div>
          ))
        }
      </dl>

      <h2>On competing views</h2>
      <p>
        Where Christians disagree, each position is summarized on its own terms: what it claims, the
        texts it leans on, who has held it, and the strongest objections to it. The aim is that an
        adherent of any view would recognize their own position in the summary.
      </p>
      <p>
        Where the author has landed on a question, that is marked separately and clearly, in a box
        like this one, so that the summary and the opinion never blur together:
      </p>
      <Callout variant="take">
        <p>
          This is what a “my take” box looks like. It sits apart from the even-handed summary
          above it, and it is always allowed to say “undecided.”
        </p>
      </Callout>
      <p>Other boxes flag notes, key texts, and cautions:</p>
      <Callout variant="scripture" title="Key text">
        <p>“For the Lord himself will descend from heaven with a cry of command…” (1 Thess. 4:16)</p>
      </Callout>
      <Callout variant="caution">
        <p>A caution box marks a common misreading or a place where the evidence is thinner than it looks.</p>
      </Callout>

      <h2>Conventions</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Scripture quotations are from the ESV unless marked otherwise.</li>
        <li>Greek and Hebrew are given in the original script with a transliteration on first use.</li>
        <li>Dates on entries show when they were written or last meaningfully revised.</li>
        <li>Every entry links to its source file, so corrections are easy to trace.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Colophon</h2>
      <p>
        Set in <em>EB Garamond</em> and <em>Cormorant Garamond</em>. Built with Astro, hosted on
        GitHub Pages, and open at <a href={SITE.repo} rel="noopener">{SITE.repo.replace('https://', '')}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .page {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    padding-top: 2.5rem;
  }
  .head {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    color: var(--vermilion);
    margin: 0 0 0.4rem;
  }
  .shelves {
    margin: 0;
    display: grid;
    gap: 1rem;
  }
  .shelf dt {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: 1.35rem;
  }
  .shelf dt a {
    color: var(--ink);
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .shelf dt a:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .shelf .initial {
    width: 2.1rem;
    height: 2.1rem;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
  }
  .shelf dd {
    margin: 0.35rem 0 0 2.85rem;
    color: var(--ink-soft);
    font-size: 1.02rem;
  }
</style>
